# Beacon Edge Server — full build spec

You are building the **ship-side edge server**. It runs on a GPU mini-PC on board (for the demo: a laptop). It serves the crew Android app and the Master's dashboard over the ship LAN and must work with **no internet**. Read `00-beacon-shared.mdc` first.

## 1. Services (docker-compose)

`edge/docker-compose.yml` with four services on one internal network:

| Service | Image / build | Port | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `db` | `pgvector/pgvector:pg16` | 5432 (internal) | volume `pgdata` |
| `model` | build `edge/model-server` | 8081 (internal) | Gemma 3n + faster-whisper + EmbeddingGemma; GPU if available (`deploy.resources.reservations.devices`), volume `models:/models` |
| `api` | build `edge/` | **8080 → host 0.0.0.0:8080** | FastAPI; also serves `dashboards/ship-web/dist` at `/` |
| `worker` | same image as `api` | — | `python -m app.workers.sync_worker` |

Also provide:
- `edge/Makefile`: `make fetch-models` (download all model weights into `./models` **before the voyage**; needs internet once), `make up`, `make seed`, `make test`, `make eval`.
- A **no-Docker dev mode**: `uvicorn app.main:app --port 8080` with `MODEL_URL` pointing at a locally running model server, so people without Docker GPU setup can work.

